<title>JAPAN: Japan July vehicle exports rise 13.3% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan July vehicle exports rise 13.3% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle exports rose 13.3 percent to 324,915 in July from a year earlier, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association (JAMA) said on Friday.</p>
<p>					(Jul exports) (yr/yr % change)</p>
<p>  Cars				  253,262	    +17.4</p>
<p>    Large			     106,082	    +19.8</p>
<p>    Compact			   146,528	    +15.4</p>
<p>    Mini				    652	   +124.1</p>
<p>  Trucks				 67,800	     -0.9</p>
<p>    Large				52,858	     +5.4</p>
<p>    Small				14,940	    -17.9</p>
<p>    Mini					2	    -93.5</p>
<p>  Buses				   3,853	    +42.6</p>
<p>  Total				 324,915	    +13.3</p>
<p>Exports by destination:</p>
<p>  Asia				   55,889	     +8.0</p>
<p>  Middle East			  22,070	   +272.7</p>
<p>  Europe				 79,786	    +10.2</p>
<p>    EU				   67,554	    +11.2</p>
<p>  North America		     106,994	    +11.1</p>
<p>    United States		   103,099	    +11.7</p>
<p>  Latin America			21,582	    -20.1</p>
<p>  Africa				 12,253	    +13.6</p>
<p>  Oceania				25,540	    +15.9</p>
<p>  Others				    801	    +30.5</p>
<p>Exports by major manufacturers:</p>
<p>  Toyota		   119,703	    +37.3</p>
<p>  Nissan		    54,932	     -1.1</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi		36,760	    -14.2</p>
<p>  Honda		     28,829	    +14.7</p>
<p>  Mazda		     34,191	    +19.9</p>
</text>
